🧠 AI Tools: Complete Guide + Pro Tips (2026)
 
A practical, categorized overview with best-use cases, selection guide, and proven techniques to avoid hallucinations & boost efficiency.
 
 
 
🗂️ Top AI Tools by Category
 
🤖 General-Purpose Assistants
 
- ChatGPT (OpenAI) 🟢: Best all-rounder; strong reasoning, multi-step tasks, large ecosystem. ✅ Free tier available.
- Claude (Anthropic) 🟠: Long documents (200k+ tokens), high-quality writing, less hallucination.
- Gemini (Google) 🔵: Live Google Search, great with multimodal (image/video), integrates Workspace.
 
🔍 Research & Fact-Finding
 
- Perplexity AI: Cited answers, web search built-in, no hallucinations; best for quick verified info.
- NotebookLM: Analyze your files only (PDF/docs/notes); grounded, no outside data.
- Elicit / Consensus: Academic/research focus; papers, summaries, evidence-based answers.
 
💻 Coding & Dev
 
- GitHub Copilot: Inline completion, VS Code/IDE integration.
- Cursor: AI-native IDE; full-project refactor, chat, agent mode.
- DeepSeek: Open-source, strong reasoning, long context .
 
🎨 Creativity & Media
 
- Images: Midjourney (quality), DALL-E 3, Ideogram (text-in-image), Adobe Firefly (safe commercial).
- Video: Runway, Pika, Kling AI.
- Audio/Voice: ElevenLabs (TTS), Whisper (transcription), Suno AI (music).
 
✍️ Writing & Docs
 
- Drafting: Claude / ChatGPT.
- Polishing: Grammarly, Hemingway Editor.
- Docs/Notes: Notion AI, NotebookLM.
 
 
 
