💡 Pro Tips for Better AI Output
 
1️⃣ Prompt Engineering Basics
 
- Be specific: Role + Goal + Context + Format + Constraints .
plaintext  
Act as senior dev → Write clean Python → Use given schema → Output JSON only → No extra text
 
- Structure: Use RAPS — Role, Audience, Purpose, Scope.
- Give examples: Show what good output looks like .
- Break big tasks: Step-by-step instead of one giant request .
 
2️⃣ Avoid Hallucinations & Errors
 
- Demand citations: “Include URL/source; flag unknowns”.
- Cross-check: Compare Perplexity + Claude + search results.
- Limit scope: Don’t overfeed; focus on your domain/data .
- Ask for reasoning: “Show your sources and logic step-by-step” .
 
3️⃣ Efficiency & Workflow Hacks
 
- Start free: Try free tiers first; upgrade only when limits hit.
- Upload context: Provide files/data instead of long copy-paste.
- Iterate: First draft → refine → fix gaps → finalize .
- Check privacy: For sensitive work, choose enterprise/self-hosted options.
 
4️⃣ Advanced Strategies
 
- Chain tools: Research → Perplexity → Draft → Claude → Edit → Grammarly.
- Self-review: Give AI a checklist: “Verify all numbers, cite sources”.
- Save prompts: Build a library for repeated tasks .
 
 
 
⚠️ Common Pitfalls to Avoid
 
❌ Blind trust: Always verify facts, code, calculations .
❌ Overly broad prompts: “Write about AI” = vague; “Write 3-paragraph summary of 2026 AI trends with 3 examples” = good.
❌ Wrong tool for job: Don’t use ChatGPT for deep file analysis; use NotebookLM.
❌ Ignoring limits: Know context window (Claude large > GPT > Gemini).
 
 
 
